---
import { t, stagger } from './util';

const cfg = stagger([
  `${t('k', 'import')} { NodeCi } ${t('k', 'from')} ${t('s', "'@acme/wf-node-ci'")};`,
  `${t('k', 'import')} { applyBaseline } ${t('k', 'from')} ${t('s', "'@cikick/policies'")};`,
  '',
  `${t('k', 'export default')} (app) ${t('p', '=>')} {`,
  `  ${t('k', 'new')} ${t('n', 'NodeCi')}(app, ${t('s', "'node'")}, {`,
  `    nodeVersion: ${t('n', '22')},`,
  `    packageManager: ${t('s', "'pnpm'")},`,
  `  });`,
  `  ${t('n', 'applyBaseline')}(app); ${t('c', '// policies')}`,
  `};`,
], 200, 110);

const tree: [number, string, string?][] = [
  [0, 'App'],
  [1, 'node', 'NodeCi'],
  [2, 'ci', 'Workflow'],
  [3, 'build', 'Job · 6 steps'],
  [3, 'test', 'Job · 5 steps'],
  [2, '.nvmrc', 'ManagedFile'],
  [2, 'renovate.json', 'ManagedFile'],
];
const treeHtml = tree
  .map(([d, id, kind], i) => `<span class="tn st" style="--d:${1500 + i * 150};--lvl:${d}"><span class="tn-id">${id}</span>${kind ? `<span class="tn-kind">${kind}</span>` : ''}</span>`)
  .join('\n');

const yml = stagger([
  t('c', '# Generated by cikick — do not edit. Run `npx cikick synth`.'),
  `${t('k', 'name')}: CI`,
  `${t('k', 'on')}: ${t('c', '# push to main, pull_request')}`,
  `${t('k', 'permissions')}:`,
  `  ${t('k', 'contents')}: read`,
  `${t('k', 'jobs')}:`,
  `  ${t('k', 'build')}:`,
  `    ${t('k', 'timeout-minutes')}: 30`,
  `    ${t('k', 'steps')}:`,
  `      - ${t('k', 'uses')}: actions/checkout@${t('h', '11d5960a3267…')} ${t('c', '# v4')}`,
  `      - ${t('k', 'uses')}: pnpm/action-setup@${t('h', 'b906affcce14…')} ${t('c', '# v4')}`,
  `      - ${t('k', 'uses')}: actions/setup-node@${t('h', '49933ea5288c…')} ${t('c', '# v4')}`,
  `      ${t('c', '# …')}`,
], 2700, 100);

const lock = stagger([
  '{',
  `  ${t('k', '"actions"')}: {`,
  `    ${t('k', '"actions/checkout@v4"')}: {`,
  `      ${t('k', '"sha"')}: ${t('h', '"11d5960a3267…"')},`,
  `      ${t('k', '"resolvedAt"')}: ${t('s', '"2026-11-22T10:36Z"')}`,
  `    }, …`,
  `  },`,
  `  ${t('k', '"packages"')}: { ${t('k', '"@acme/wf-node-ci"')}: ${t('s', '"2.0.0"')} }`,
  '}',
], 4000, 90);
---
<section id="idea" class="sec sec-alt" aria-labelledby="idea-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
    <h2 id="idea-title">Constructs in. Pinned YAML out.</h2>
    <p class="sec-lede">
      Like AWS CDK, but for workflows. You describe CI as typed TypeScript objects; <code>cikick synth</code> walks the
      construct tree and writes plain <code>.github/workflows/*.yml</code>, resolves every action to a commit SHA, and records it in
      <code>cikick.lock.json</code>. The generated YAML runs without cikick; <code>cikick check</code> is an optional CI gate. Stop using cikick and the committed YAML keeps working.
    </p>

    <div class="pipe" data-anim id="pipe" role="group" aria-labelledby="pipe-cap">
      <div class="pipe-col">
        <h3 class="pipe-h"><span class="num">1</span> You write <code>cikick.config.ts</code></h3>
        <div class="code-win"><div class="win-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>cikick.config.ts</b></div>
          <pre class="code" set:html={cfg}></pre></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipe-link" aria-hidden="true"><span class="chip-cmd">cikick synth</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 16" width="40" height="16"><path d="M0 8h34m-7-6 7 6-7 6" /></svg></div>
      <div class="pipe-col">
        <h3 class="pipe-h"><span class="num">2</span> Constructs form a tree</h3>
        <div class="tree" aria-hidden="true" set:html={treeHtml}></div>
        <p class="mini">Aspects visit every node: add permissions, timeouts, rewrite deprecated actions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipe-link" aria-hidden="true"><span class="chip-cmd">render + pin</span><svg viewBox="0 0 40 16" width="40" height="16"><path d="M0 8h34m-7-6 7 6-7 6" /></svg></div>
      <div class="pipe-col">
        <h3 class="pipe-h"><span class="num">3</span> YAML and a lockfile</h3>
        <div class="code-win"><div class="win-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>.github/workflows/ci.yml</b></div>
          <pre class="code sm" set:html={yml}></pre></div>
        <div class="code-win lock"><div class="win-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>cikick.lock.json</b></div>
          <pre class="code sm" set:html={lock}></pre></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p id="pipe-cap" class="sr-only">
      A cikick.config.ts file that instantiates a NodeCi construct is turned into a construct tree (App, NodeCi, Workflow, two Jobs and two managed files), then rendered to ci.yml where every action is pinned to a commit SHA with a version comment, plus a cikick.lock.json recording each resolved SHA.
    </p>
    <button class="replay" type="button" data-replay="pipe">Replay</button>

    <ul class="points">
      <li><b>Typed props</b> instead of YAML anchors and string templating. A breaking change fails at compile time.</li>
      <li><b>Distributed as npm packages.</b> Your platform team ships <code>@acme/wf-node-ci</code>; repos depend on it like any library.</li>
      <li><b>Every repo can still deviate</b> through props, escape hatches (<code>addOverride</code>) and aspects. No fork needed.</li>
      <li><b>Reviewable.</b> Generated YAML is committed, and <code>cikick check</code> fails CI if it drifts from the config.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
